# Machine-generated tool/cache artifacts only. Runtime data dirs
# (input/state/output) are user-defined and live outside the repo
# (design.md §4.7.7).

# Python / tooling
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/

# Dev-tool caches (same rationale -- machine-generated, never meant to
# be committed).
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Quickstart demo runtime scratch (docs/usage.md「開箱即用快速驗證」,
# docker/example/README.md). The committed docker/example/{input,state}
# fixtures are the pristine SOURCE; the quickstart copies the seed into
# docker/example/run/state and writes the deliverable to
# docker/example/run/output, so a demo run never mutates the committed
# fixtures nor drops output/.lock/runs.jsonl into the committed tree
# (design.md §4.7.7 pristine-fixture guarantee). This is the sole in-repo
# runtime location and is never committed.
docker/example/run/
